; A posting with a number left to interpolation adds nothing to the
; tolerance its transaction's residual is checked against. The 0.00 USD
; with a cost to interpolate does not widen USD to 0.005, so 0.004 USD is
; a residual; the -10.5 EUR with a price to interpolate does not widen EUR
; to 0.05, so 0.04 EUR is one; and with only whole numbers written there is
; no tolerance at all for what the interpolated price leaves.
2020-01-01 open Assets:A
2020-01-01 open Assets:B
2020-01-01 open Expenses:B

2020-01-02 * "a cost to interpolate on zero units"
  Expenses:B  0.00 USD {2020-01-01}
  Assets:A   -0.004 USD

2020-01-03 * "a price to interpolate"
  Assets:A  -10.5 EUR @ USD
  Assets:B   1.04 EUR
  Assets:B  -1 EUR

2020-01-04 * "whole numbers only"
  Assets:A  -3 EUR @ USD
  Assets:B   10 USD

2020-01-05 * "stated numbers still widen it"
  Assets:A   10.00 USD
  Assets:B  -10.004 USD
